## 3. Competitive Analysis & Research Insights

### 3.1 Competitive Landscape

| Product | Type | Strengths | Weaknesses | ShramikSetu Advantage |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| e-Shram (Govt.) | National worker registry | Scale, govt backing | Static registration only | We add per-project workflow |
| WorkIndia | Job marketplace | Large worker pool | No wage tracking or compliance | We track full employment lifecycle |
| BetterPlace | Workforce platform | Compliance tools | Enterprise-focused, expensive | We target small contractors |
| Haqdarshak | Welfare scheme discovery | Scheme matching | No employment record | We create the employment record |
| Paper registers | Incumbent "solution" | Zero cost | Zero accountability | Digital permanence |

### 3.2 Research Insights

| Insight | Source | Design Implication |
|---|---|---|
| 76% of construction workers receive wages in cash | NSS 2019-20 | Payment ledger records contractor's declaration, not verified transfers |
| Most workers own basic Android smartphones (₹8K-12K) | TRAI 2024 | Mobile-responsive web, not native app. Low bandwidth optimization |
| Worker digital literacy: WhatsApp, QR scan, PIN entry | Field observation | Interaction model: scan → enter PIN → confirm. No complex forms |
| Contractors manage 10-40 workers per site | Industry interviews | Batch operations, simple payroll view |
| Labour inspectors cover 1000+ establishments each | Labour Bureau data | Risk-prioritized dashboard, not exhaustive listing |
| Minimum wages vary by state and occupation | State notifications | Reference table, not legal assertion |

### 3.3 Policy Alignment

| Initiative | Relationship |
|---|---|
| e-Shram | Complementary. ShramikSetu stores e-Shram UAN as optional field. No API integration in MVP. |
| BOCW Welfare Boards | Complementary. Employment Passport could support welfare claims (future). |
| Minimum Wages Act, 1948 | Reference only. System displays configurable wage rates. Does not make legal determinations. |
| Contract Labour Act, 1970 | Contextual. System digitizes the contractor-worker relationship the Act regulates. |

> **Disclaimer:** ShramikSetu is an academic prototype. It does not claim government endorsement, legal authority, or regulatory compliance certification.

