## 8. Module Specifications

> **Convention:** Each module follows a standardized template. Modules are numbered M-01 through M-14.

---

### M-01: Authentication & Role Management

**Purpose:** Provide secure email/password authentication with role-based access control for 4 roles.

**Business Goal:** Establish the identity foundation that all other modules depend on.

**Actors:** All users (Worker, Supervisor, Contractor, Inspector).

**Preconditions:** User has a valid email address.

**User Story:**
> As a new user, I want to register with my email and select my role, so that I can access the features relevant to me.

**Main Workflow:**

| Step | Actor | Action | System Response |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | User | Navigate to `/register` | Registration form displayed |
| 2 | User | Enter name, email, password, phone, role | Client-side validation runs |
| 3 | User | Submit form | POST to Supabase Auth |
| 4 | System | Validate inputs | Check email uniqueness, password strength |
| 5 | System | Create user record | Insert into `users` with role |
| 6 | System | Issue JWT | Token contains `user_id`, `role`, `email` |
| 7 | System | Redirect | To role-specific dashboard |
| 8 | User | Subsequent requests | JWT sent in `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header |
| 9 | System | Validate on every API call | Middleware checks JWT signature + role permission |

**Alternative Flow:**

| Scenario | Handling |
|---|---|
| Email already registered | 409 Conflict: "This email is already registered. Please login." |
| Invalid password format | 400: "Password must be ≥ 8 characters with 1 number and 1 special character" |
| Forgot password | Supabase sends reset email. User clicks link, sets new password. |
| Expired JWT | 401: "Session expired. Please login again." Frontend redirects to `/login`. |

**Edge Cases:**

| Edge Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| User tries to register with Inspector role | Blocked. Inspector accounts are created by Admin only. |
| User refreshes page mid-registration | Form data lost (acceptable for MVP). |
| Concurrent registration with same email | DB unique constraint prevents duplicate. Second request gets 409. |
| JWT token tampered | Signature validation fails. 401 returned. |

**Acceptance Criteria:**

- [ ] User can register with email, password, name, phone, role (Worker/Supervisor/Contractor)
- [ ] Inspector role can only be assigned by existing Admin
- [ ] Login returns JWT; invalid credentials return 401
- [ ] Role is embedded in JWT claims and validated on every request
