### M-07: Payment Ledger

**Purpose:** Record contractor's payment declarations to workers, creating a transparent, auditable transaction history.

**Business Goal:** Replace "I paid you" / "No you didn't" disputes with a permanent digital record.

**Actors:** Contractor (records payment), Worker (views), Inspector (views).

**Preconditions:** Wage record exists. Worker has active contract.

**User Story:**
> As a contractor, I want to record that I paid a worker, so that there is a permanent record of the transaction that protects both of us.

> As a worker, I want to see a record of every payment made to me, so that I can verify and contest if needed.

**Design Decision – Ledger, Not Wallet:**

| Wallet (removed) | Ledger (MVP) |
|---|---|
| Has balance | No balance |
| Requires top-up | No top-up |
| Simulated money transfer | Records payment declaration |
| Complex state management | Simple insert-only records |
| Implies real money flow | Clearly a record-keeping tool |

The Payment Ledger is a **record of declared payments**. The contractor states "I paid ₹X to Worker Y for Period Z." The system records it. It does not process or verify actual money transfer.

**Main Workflow:**

| Step | Actor | Action | System Response |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Contractor | Navigate to Payments → Select project | Shows workers with pending wages |
| 2 | Contractor | Select worker | Shows expected wage, days worked |
| 3 | Contractor | Enter amount paid | Pre-filled with expected wage (editable) |
| 4 | Contractor | Enter payment method | Cash / UPI / Bank Transfer / Other |
| 5 | Contractor | Enter payment date | Default: today |
| 6 | Contractor | Optional: Add note | E.g., "Includes ₹200 bonus" |
| 7 | Contractor | Submit | Payment record created |
| 8 | System | Update wage_record status | `PAID_FULL` or `UNDERPAID` |
| 9 | System | Write Audit Log | `payment.recorded` |
| 10 | System | Notify worker | "Payment of ₹X recorded for [period]" |
| 11 | System | Update Employment Passport | Payment added to history |

**Alternative Flow:**

| Scenario | Handling |
|---|---|
| Contractor enters amount > expected wage | Allowed. Status: `OVERPAID`. Warning shown. |
| Contractor enters amount = 0 | Blocked: "Amount must be > 0. If no payment made, don't record." |
| Contractor tries to edit recorded payment | Blocked. Payments are immutable. Correction via dispute. |
| Worker disputes a payment | Dispute links to payment record. Inspector reviews. |

**Edge Cases:**

| Edge Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| Multiple payments to same worker for same period | Allowed (installments). Total tracked. |
| Contractor records payment for worker with no attendance | Warning: "No attendance records for this period. Proceed?" |
| Payment date in future | Blocked: "Payment date cannot be in the future." |
| Contractor records payment after project ended | Allowed. Late payments are valid. |

**Acceptance Criteria:**

- [ ] Contractor records payment with amount, method, date, note
- [ ] Amount pre-filled from expected wage (editable)
- [ ] Payment record is immutable after creation
- [ ] Wage record status updates automatically
- [ ] Worker sees payment in history
