### M-09: Attendance & Payment Disputes

**Purpose:** Provide workers a structured mechanism to contest attendance errors or payment issues, with resolution by Labour Inspector.

**Business Goal:** Replace informal, unresolved grievances with a tracked, auditable dispute workflow.

**Actors:** Worker (raises), Contractor (responds), Inspector (resolves).

**Preconditions:** Worker has an attendance record or payment record to dispute.

**User Story:**
> As a worker, I want to raise a dispute when my attendance is wrong or my payment is less than expected, so that an authority can review and resolve it.

**Main Workflow:**

| Step | Actor | Action | System Response |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Worker | Navigate to attendance/payment → Click "Raise Dispute" | Dispute form opens |
| 2 | Worker | Select dispute type | `attendance_error` / `payment_underpaid` / `payment_missing` / `other` |
| 3 | Worker | Write description | Text, max 500 chars |
| 4 | System | Auto-link evidence | Attendance record, payment record, wage calculation |
| 5 | Worker | Submit | Dispute created, status: `open` |
| 6 | System | Notify contractor + inspector | In-app + email |
| 7 | System | Write Audit Log | `dispute.raised` |
| 8 | Contractor | View dispute, optionally respond | Response saved, status: `contractor_responded` |
| 9 | Inspector | View dispute queue | Sorted by priority, filterable |
| 10 | Inspector | Review evidence | Attendance, payments, audit trail |
| 11 | Inspector | Resolve | `upheld` / `dismissed` / `partial` + notes |
| 12 | System | If upheld: adjust records | Update attendance or flag payment for correction |
| 13 | System | Notify all parties | Resolution communicated |
| 14 | System | Write Audit Log | `dispute.resolved` |

**Dispute Data Model:**

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| dispute_id | UUID (PK) | |
| worker_id | UUID (FK) | Who raised it |
| contractor_id | UUID (FK) | Against whom |
| project_id | UUID (FK) | Related project |
| dispute_type | Enum | attendance_error, payment_underpaid, payment_missing, contract_violation, other |
| description | Text | Worker's complaint |
| linked_attendance_id | UUID (FK, nullable) | If attendance dispute |
| linked_payment_id | UUID (FK, nullable) | If payment dispute |
| status | Enum | open, contractor_responded, under_review, resolved, closed |
| priority | Enum | low, medium, high |
| contractor_response | Text, nullable | Contractor's side |
| resolution_notes | Text, nullable | Inspector's decision |
| outcome | Enum, nullable | upheld, dismissed, partial |
| resolved_by | UUID (FK, nullable) | Inspector who resolved |
| raised_at | Timestamp | |
| resolved_at | Timestamp, nullable | |

**Alternative Flow:**

| Scenario | Handling |
|---|---|
| Worker raises duplicate dispute for same record | Blocked: "A dispute for this record already exists." |
| Contractor doesn't respond within 7 days | Dispute escalates to inspector queue. Status: `under_review`. |
| Inspector upholds attendance dispute | Attendance status changed. Wage recalculated. |
| Inspector upholds payment dispute | Payment flagged. Contractor notified to correct. |

**Edge Cases:**

| Edge Case | Handling |
|---|---|
| Worker raises dispute for another worker's record | Blocked by RBAC. Can only dispute own records. |
| Dispute raised after project ended | Allowed. Historical disputes are valid. |
| Multiple disputes for same payment | Allowed if different issues. Linked to same payment_id. |
| Inspector resolves dispute but worker disagrees | Worker can raise a new dispute. No appeal mechanism in MVP. |

**Acceptance Criteria:**

- [ ] Worker raises dispute from attendance or payment record
- [ ] Dispute includes type, description, auto-linked evidence
- [ ] Contractor notified and can respond
- [ ] Inspector sees dispute queue sorted by priority
- [ ] Inspector resolves with notes; resolution logged
- [ ] If upheld, related record is adjusted
- [ ] Full audit trail maintained
- [ ] All parties notified of resolution
- [ ] Dispute text translatable in 3 languages

**API Endpoints:**

| Method | Endpoint | Auth | Role | Description |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| POST | `/api/v1/disputes` | Bearer | Worker | Raise dispute |
| GET | `/api/v1/disputes/me` | Bearer | Worker | My disputes |
| GET | `/api/v1/disputes` | Bearer | Inspector | All disputes (queue) |
| GET | `/api/v1/disputes/{id}` | Bearer | All | Dispute detail |
| POST | `/api/v1/disputes/{id}/respond` | Bearer | Contractor | Respond to dispute |
| PUT | `/api/v1/disputes/{id}/resolve` | Bearer | Inspector | Resolve dispute |

**Database Tables Used:** `disputes`, `attendance`, `payment_ledger`, `wage_records`, `workers`, `contractors`, `notifications`, `audit_logs`

**UI Screens:**
- Raise Dispute form (worker): Type, description, linked evidence preview
- My Disputes list (worker): Status badges, timeline
- Dispute Detail: Full context, responses, resolution
- Dispute Queue (inspector): Sortable, filterable table
- Dispute Resolution form (inspector): Outcome, notes

**Validation Rules:**

| Field | Rule |
|---|---|
| dispute_type | Required, enum |
| description | Required, 10-500 chars |
| linked record | Must exist and belong to worker |
| contractor_response | Optional, max 1000 chars |
| resolution_notes | Required on resolve, min 10 chars |

**Future Enhancements:**
- Worker appeal mechanism
- Dispute escalation to higher authority
- Evidence upload (photos, documents)
- Dispute analytics and patterns

