### M-14: GPS Geofencing (Integrated with Attendance)

> **Note:** GPS Geofencing is not a standalone module. It is a sub-feature of M-05 (Attendance). This section provides the detailed technical specification.

**Purpose:** Verify that the worker is physically present at the project site when marking attendance.

**Business Goal:** Prevent proxy attendance and location fraud without requiring hardware.

**Actors:** Worker (provides location), System (validates).

**Preconditions:** Project has GPS coordinates and radius configured.

**User Story:**
> As a contractor, I want attendance to be verified against the project site location, so that workers can't mark attendance from home.

**Technical Specification:**

**Project Location Data:**

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| project_id | UUID (FK) | |
| latitude | Decimal(10, 8) | Site center |
| longitude | Decimal(11, 8) | Site center |
| radius_m | Integer | Allowed attendance radius (50-500m, default 200m) |
| address | Text | Human-readable site address |
| set_by | UUID (FK) | Who set the location |
| is_manual | Boolean | True if manually entered, False if auto-detected |

**Attendance Verification Data:**

| Field | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| verification_id | UUID (PK) | |
| attendance_id | UUID (FK) | |
| worker_latitude | Decimal(10, 8) | Worker's GPS at time of marking |
| worker_longitude | Decimal(11, 8) | |
| distance_from_site_m | Decimal(10, 2) | Haversine result |
| within_radius | Boolean | |
| gps_accuracy_m | Decimal(6, 2) | Browser-reported accuracy |
| verification_method | Enum | `pin_gps`, `pin_only`, `supervisor_override` |
| override_reason | Text, nullable | If supervisor overrode |
| overridden_by | UUID (FK, nullable) | Supervisor who overrode |
| verified_at | Timestamp | |

**Haversine Calculation:**

The backend calculates distance using the Haversine formula. This is a pure mathematical function—no external API calls.

```python
def haversine_distance(lat1: float, lon1: float, lat2: float, lon2: float) -> float:
    """Calculate distance in meters between two GPS coordinates."""
    R = 6_371_000  # Earth's radius in meters
    phi1, phi2 = math.radians(lat1), math.radians(lat2)
    dphi = math.radians(lat2 - lat1)
    dlambda = math.radians(lon2 - lon1)
    a = math.sin(dphi/2)**2 + math.cos(phi1)*math.cos(phi2)*math.sin(dlambda/2)**2
    return R * 2 * math.atan2(math.sqrt(a), math.sqrt(1-a))
```

**Verification Flow:**

```
Worker enters PIN
       ↓
Browser requests GPS permission
       ↓
  ┌─ Permission granted ──────────────────────────┐
  │                                                │
  │  Browser returns lat/lng + accuracy            │
  │         ↓                                      │
  │  POST /attendance/mark {pin, lat, lng}         │
  │         ↓                                      │
  │  Backend: Validate PIN                         │
  │  Backend: Haversine(worker, project)           │
  │         ↓                                      │
  │  ┌─ distance ≤ radius ──┐                      │
  │  │  ✅ ATTENDANCE MARKED │                     │
  │  │  method: pin_gps      │                     │
  │  └───────────────────────┘                     │
  │  ┌─ distance > radius ──┐                      │
  │  │  ❌ BLOCKED           │                     │
  │  │  Show distance        │                     │
  │  │  Offer override       │                     │
  │  └───────────────────────┘                     │
  │                                                │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
  ┌─ Permission denied ───────────────────────────┐
  │                                                │
  │  Show explanation of why GPS needed            │
  │  Option 1: Retry with permission               │
  │  Option 2: PIN-only (flagged for review)       │
  │                                                │
  └────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**What GPS Geofencing Does NOT Include:**

| Excluded | Reason |
|---|---|
| Live/continuous GPS tracking | Privacy violation; unnecessary |
| Background location monitoring | Requires native app; web can't do this |
| Route history | Not needed for attendance |
| GPS replay analytics | Over-engineering for MVP |
| Multiple geofence zones | Future scope |
| Dynamic geofencing | Future scope |
| Supervisor live location | Future scope |

**Privacy Considerations:**

| Aspect | Handling |
|---|---|
| GPS data collection | Only during attendance marking. Not continuous. |
| Data storage | Lat/lng stored with attendance record. Not shared. |
| User consent | Browser permission dialog. Clear explanation. |
| Data retention | Stored as part of attendance record. Subject to same retention. |
| Worker can see what's stored | Yes, in attendance history. |

**Acceptance Criteria:**

- [ ] Project location (lat/lng/radius) configurable at creation
- [ ] Browser GPS permission requested during attendance
- [ ] Haversine distance calculated server-side
- [ ] Within radius → attendance marked
- [ ] Outside radius → blocked with distance shown
- [ ] GPS denied → PIN-only fallback with flag
- [ ] Override requires supervisor credentials + reason
- [ ] All verification data stored (lat, lng, distance, accuracy, method)
- [ ] No continuous tracking
- [ ] No background location access

**Future Enhancements:**
- Multiple work zones per project
- Dynamic radius adjustment by supervisor
- Supervisor location verification
- Photo + GPS combined verification
- Device integrity checks (anti-spoofing)

