## 11. Security Model

### 11.1 Authentication

| Aspect | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Method | Email + password via Supabase Auth |
| Password storage | Bcrypt hash (Supabase managed) |
| Session token | JWT (HS256), 24-hour expiry |
| Token storage | httpOnly cookie (preferred) or localStorage |
| Token validation | Every API request validated by FastAPI middleware |
| Password policy | Min 8 chars, 1 digit, 1 special char |
| Brute force protection | Supabase rate limiting: 5 failed attempts → 15 min lockout |

### 11.2 Authorization (RBAC)

| Layer | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Route level | FastAPI dependency injection checks role before handler |
| Data level | Supabase RLS policies restrict row access |
| API level | Each endpoint declares allowed roles |
| Frontend level | Route guards redirect unauthorized access |

### 11.3 Data Protection

| Aspect | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Encryption in transit | TLS 1.3 (HTTPS enforced) |
| Encryption at rest | Supabase default (AES-256) |
| GPS data | Stored with attendance; not shared externally |
| Passwords | Never stored in plaintext |
| PIN codes | SHA-256 hashed before storage |
| JWT secret | Environment variable; never in code |
| API keys | Environment variables; `.env` in `.gitignore` |

### 11.4 Input Validation

| Layer | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Frontend | Client-side validation for UX |
| Backend | Pydantic models enforce types, ranges, formats |
| Database | Constraints (NOT NULL, UNIQUE, CHECK, FK) |
| API | Request schema validation before processing |

### 11.5 Rate Limiting

| Endpoint Category | Limit |
|---|---|
| Auth (login, register) | 5 requests/min per IP |
| Attendance marking | 5 attempts/day per worker |
| PDF generation | 1 request/30s per user |
| General API | 100 requests/min per user |

### 11.6 Audit & Accountability

| Aspect | Implementation |
|---|---|
| Action logging | Every state change logged to `audit_logs` |
| Immutability | Audit logs are append-only (no UPDATE/DELETE) |
| IP logging | Request IP stored with each audit entry |
| Data access | Inspector/Admin only for audit logs |

### 11.7 Security Considerations for GPS

| Concern | Mitigation |
|---|---|
| GPS spoofing | MVP: Accept browser GPS. Log accuracy. Flag anomalies. Future: Device integrity. |
| Location privacy | GPS collected only during attendance. Not continuous. User consent via browser. |
| Man-in-the-middle | HTTPS enforced. |
| Replay attacks | Timestamp validation (± 5 min). |

